se data-c=\"1D435\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D435\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(170.5,272)\"><use data-c=\"20D7\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-20D7\"></use></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1757.9,0)\"><use data-c=\"22C5\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-22C5\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(2258.1,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mover\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D451\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D451\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(194.3,283)\"><use data-c=\"20D7\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-20D7\"></use></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(2952.4,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D459\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D459\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(3528.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(4583.9,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D707\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D707\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(636,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-30\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(5623.5,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D43C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43C\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></td>\n  </tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></p>\n<p>Choose the correct answer from the options given below:</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"A-III, B-IV, C-I, D-II\n"},{"identifier":"B","content":"A-IV, B-II, C-III, D-I\n"},{"identifier":"C","content":"A-II, B-III, C-IV, D-I\n"},{"identifier":"D","content":"A-I, B-III, C-IV, D-II"}],"correct_options":["C"],"explanation":"<p>Let's identify each law listed in List I and match it with the corresponding mathematical expression listed in List II.</p>\n\n<strong>Gauss's law of magnetostatics</strong> states that the total magnetic flux through a closed surface is zero, as magnetic monopoles do not exist. This is given by the formula:\n\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.691ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"11.637ex\" height=\"3.173ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -1097 5143.7 1402.5\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(0 0.5)\"><use data-c=\"222E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-SO-222E\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(776.7,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mover\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D435\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D435\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(170.5,272)\"><use data-c=\"20D7\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-20D7\"></use></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1757.9,0)\"><use data-c=\"22C5\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-22C5\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(2258.1,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mover\"><g data-mml-node=\"mrow\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D451\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D451\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(523,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D44E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D44E\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(276,283)\"><use data-c=\"20D7\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-20D7\"></use></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(3587.9,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(4643.7,0)\"><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-30\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></p>\n\n<p>So, (A) matches with (II).</p>\n\n<strong>Faraday's law of electromagnetic induction</strong> states that the induced electromotive force (emf) in any closed loop is equal to the negative of the time rate of change of the magnetic flux through the loop. It is given by:\n\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.798ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"22.031ex\" height=\"3.28ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -1097 9737.5 1449.8\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(0 0.5)\"><use data-c=\"222E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-SO-222E\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(776.7,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mover\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D438\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D438\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(233.5,269)\"><use data-c=\"20D7\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-20D7\"></use></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1762.9,0)\"><use data-c=\"22C5\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-22C5\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(2263.1,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mover\"><g data-mml-node=\"mrow\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D451\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D451\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(523,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D459\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D459\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(160.5,283)\"><use data-c=\"20D7\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-20D7\"></use></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(3361.9,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(4417.7,0)\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\" transform=\"translate(5195.7,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(347.6,394) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D451\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D451\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mrow\" transform=\"translate(220,-345) scale(0.707)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D451\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D451\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(523,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D461\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D461\"></use></g></g><rect width=\"825.1\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(6427.4,0) translate(0 0.5)\"><use data-c=\"222B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-SO-222B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(7204.1,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mover\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D435\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D435\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(170.5,272)\"><use data-c=\"20D7\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-20D7\"></use></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(8185.3,0)\"><use data-c=\"22C5\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-22C5\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(8685.5,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mover\"><g data-mml-node=\"mrow\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D451\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D451\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(523,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D44E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D44E\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(276,283)\"><use data-c=\"20D7\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-20D7\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></p>\n\n<p>Hence, (B) matches with (III).</p>\n\n<strong>Ampere's law</strong> relates the integrated magnetic field around a closed loop to the electric current passing through the loop. The mathematical expression given in the context of magnetostatics (without the displacement current) is:\n\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.691ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"13.476ex\" height=\"3.173ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -1097 5956.2 1402.5\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(0 0.5)\"><use data-c=\"222E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-SO-222E\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(776.7,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mover\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D435\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D435\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(170.5,272)\"><use data-c=\"20D7\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-20D7\"></use></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1757.9,0)\"><use data-c=\"22C5\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-22C5\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(2258.1,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mover\"><g data-mml-node=\"mrow\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D451\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D451\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(523,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D459\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D459\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(160.5,283)\"><use data-c=\"20D7\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-20D7\"></use></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(3356.9,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(4412.7,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D707\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D707\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(636,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-30\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(5452.2,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D43C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43C\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></p>\n\n<p>Consequently, (C) matches with (IV).</p>\n\n<p>Lastly, <strong>Gauss's law of electrostatics</strong> states that the total electric flux out of a closed surface is proportional to the charge enclosed within the surface:</p>\n\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -1.045ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"19.184ex\" height=\"3.527ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -1097 8479.2 1559.1\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(0 0.5)\"><use data-c=\"222E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-SO-222E\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(776.7,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mover\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D438\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D438\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(233.5,269)\"><use data-c=\"20D7\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-20D7\"></use></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1762.9,0)\"><use data-c=\"22C5\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-22C5\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(2263.1,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mover\"><g data-mml-node=\"mrow\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D451\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D451\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(523,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D44E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D44E\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(276,283)\"><use data-c=\"20D7\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-20D7\"></use></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(3592.9,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\" transform=\"translate(4648.7,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(362.3,394) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(220,-345) scale(0.707)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D700\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D700\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(499,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-30\"></use></g></g>